# OpenRobOps configs

This folder contains YAML files that need to be applied to OpenRobOps to configure data sources,
actions and other settings in OpenRobOps specific to this flatland simulation.

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `config.yaml` | key-value and ROS-diagnostics data sources, robot/fleet/welcome/navigation dashboards, battery/dock/message actions, ROS agentlet ModuleStates, statuses and incidents |
| `maps.yaml` | a rendered "pretty" version of the simulation map as a shared `SpatialAnnotation`, shown next to the robot's own occupancy grid |
| `footprint.yaml` | the fleet-wide `RobotFootprint` (nav2's 0.44 x 0.28 m rectangle enlarged to 0.60 x 0.38 m, rounded corners), so the Navigation widget draws the robot's real outline instead of the default ring |
| `paths.yaml` | the fleet-wide `RobotPath` styling for nav2's planned paths: `"0"` (global plan, `/plan`) and `"1"` (local trajectory) |

## Welcome page content

The Welcome dashboard uses seven text widgets across three sections:

**Intro section** (no title)

| File | Layout | Content |
|------|--------|---------|
| `welcome-intro.md` | full width | Welcome heading and OpenRobOps intro |

**Dashboards section**

| File | Layout | Content |
|------|--------|---------|
| `welcome-fleet.md` | 4 columns | Fleet dashboard description |
| `welcome-robot.md` | 4 columns | Robot dashboard description |
| `welcome-navigation.md` | 4 columns | Navigation dashboard description |

**Simulation section**

| File | Layout | Content |
|------|--------|---------|
| `welcome-simulation-map.md` | 6 columns | Simulation details and ASCII map |
| `welcome-action.md` | 6 columns | Commands and key-value telemetry |
| `welcome-footer.md` | full width | GitHub / docker environment link |

After editing any file, regenerate `config.yaml`:

```
node embed-welcome-content.mjs
```

## Apply configs

Use the ORO CLI (`pipx install oro-cli`), pointed at your ORO:
```
oro context add local --url http://localhost:3000/api --api-key <API_KEY>
oro apply -f config.yaml
oro apply -f maps.yaml
oro apply -f footprint.yaml
oro apply -f paths.yaml
```
